## 3. Introduction to ABI

ABI stands for Application Binary Interface.

It defines the conventions that allow separately compiled software components to work together correctly.

The ABI specifies:

- Function argument passing.
- Return-value handling.
- Register usage.
- Stack organization.
- Data type representation.
- Function calling conventions.

### ISA vs ABI

| ISA | ABI |
|---|---|
| Instruction Set Architecture | Application Binary Interface |
| Defines processor instructions | Defines software interaction conventions |
| Specifies supported operations | Specifies calling and register conventions |
| Hardware instruction interface | Binary software interface |

