## 5. RISC-V Calling Convention

The calling convention defines how a function receives arguments, returns results, and manages registers.

Under the standard RISC-V integer calling convention:

- a0-a7 are used for passing integer arguments.
- a0-a1 are used for returning values.
- ra holds the return address.
- sp maintains the stack pointer.
- s0-s11 are callee-saved registers.
- t0-t6 are temporary caller-saved registers.

### Caller-Saved Registers

Caller-saved registers may be modified by the called function.

The caller must preserve any values it needs after the function call.

### Callee-Saved Registers

Callee-saved registers must be restored by the called function if it modifies them.

