## 6. Stack Organization

The stack is a memory region used during function execution.

It stores information such as:

- Saved registers.
- Return addresses.
- Local variables.
- Temporary data.

The stack pointer (sp) identifies the current stack position.

In the standard RISC-V ABI, the stack grows toward lower memory addresses and must be aligned to a 16-byte boundary at procedure entry.

![Stack Frame](images/stack_frame.png)

