## 8. C Program and RISC-V Assembly

A C function can be translated into RISC-V assembly using the GNU compiler toolchain.

### Example C Program

```c
int add_numbers(int a, int b)
{
    return a + b;
}

int main(void)
{
    int result = add_numbers(10, 20);
    return result;
}
```

The function receives two arguments and returns the result.

According to the standard integer calling convention:

- The first argument is passed in a0.
- The second argument is passed in a1.
- The result is returned in a0.

### Example Assembly Instructions

```asm
add_numbers:
    add a0, a0, a1
    ret
```

This adds the values in a0 and a1 and places the result in a0.

**Note:** This is an illustrative assembly example. Actual compiler-generated assembly may contain additional instructions depending on compiler options and target settings.

