## 9. Compilation and Disassembly

The GNU RISC-V compiler can generate assembly output from C source code.

### Generate Assembly

```bash
riscv64-unknown-elf-gcc -S -O0 \
-march=rv64i -mabi=lp64 \
code/main.c -o assembly/main.s
```

### Generate Object File

```bash
riscv64-unknown-elf-gcc -c -O0 \
-march=rv64i -mabi=lp64 \
code/main.c -o outputs/main.o
```

### Inspect Disassembly

```bash
riscv64-unknown-elf-objdump -d outputs/main.o
```

Save the output:

```bash
riscv64-unknown-elf-objdump -d outputs/main.o \
> outputs/disassembly.txt
```

![Disassembly Output](images/disassembly_output.png)

**Note:** These commands assume the matching RV64 bare-metal compiler is installed. If you use a different compiler or ABI, adjust the target flags accordingly.

